# Obsidian Brain MCP Configuration
# Export these values before starting the server or add them to your MCP
# client's `env` configuration. The server does not load .env files itself.
# Register the CLI in Obsidian: Settings > General > Advanced > turn
# "Command line interface" on, then accept the prompt to register it in PATH.
# Linux copies the bundled `obsidian-cli` to ~/.local/bin/obsidian (mode 755);
# keep ~/.local/bin on PATH. Windows appends the install directory to the user
# PATH; macOS links it into /usr/local/bin. Verify with `obsidian version`, which
# prints e.g. `1.12.7 (installer 1.12.7)`.

# Vault resolution order:
# 1) vault= argument sent when OBSIDIAN_VAULT is set
# 2) calling process CWD when it is inside a registered vault
# 3) most recently focused open vault window
# 4) otherwise: Vault not found.
# If OBSIDIAN_VAULT is unset, the vault MUST be open in Obsidian. Set it to the
# vault folder name or id from ~/.config/obsidian/obsidian.json for reliability;
# Obsidian opens that vault's window on demand.
# Application failures are reported as a line on STDOUT with exit code 0
# (for example, `Vault not found.`).
# Only a CLI binary failure to reach Obsidian uses exit code 1 and STDERR:
# `The CLI is unable to find Obsidian. Please make sure Obsidian is running and try again.`

# Optional: vault folder name or id, not a filesystem path.
# OBSIDIAN_VAULT=My Vault

# Optional: executable path when `obsidian` is not available on PATH.
# OBSIDIAN_CLI_PATH=/full/path/to/obsidian
